<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>8.7.4: Finding the Missing Terms</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02191</md:content-id>
    <md:title>8.7.4: Finding the Missing Terms</md:title>
    <md:uuid>b267ba51-7bfc-499b-84de-5ed2617e5b13</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Student Activity</title>
<para>Here are pairs of equivalent expressions in standard form and factored form. Find the missing symbols and numbers.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x^2 \;\square\; 16x \;\square\; 17\) and \((x + 1)(x − 17)\)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> − and –. The completed expression is \(x^2− 16x − 17\).</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x^2 \;\square\; 16x\; \square\; 17\) and \((x − 1)(x + 17)\)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> + and −, respectively. The completed expression is \(x^2+16x −17\).</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x^2+3x −28\) and \((x + \square)(x − \square)\)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 7 and 4, respectively. The completed expression is \((x + 7)(x − 4)\).</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x^2−12x −28\) and \((x \;\square \;\square)(x \;\square \;\square)\)</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> −14 and +2. The completed expression is \((x − 14)(x + 2)\).</para></section>
</content>
